
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <title>Background Image Program</title>

    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">

    <!-- Bootstrap CSS -->
    <link href="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap@5.3.3/dist/css/bootstrap.min.css"
          rel="stylesheet">

    <style>

      
    <style>
        body {
            margin: 0;
            padding: 0;
            min-height: 100vh;
            background-image: url("image12.jpg");
            background-repeat: no-repeat;
            background-size: cover;
            background-position: center;
            background-attachment: fixed;
        }

        h1 {
            color: white;
            text-align: center;
            padding-top: 100px;
            font-size: 50px;
        }

        p {
            color: white;
            text-align: center;
            font-size: 25px;
        }
   
    </style>
</head>

<body>

<div class="container content">

    <h1 class="text-center text-primary">
        Background Image in Bootstrap
    </h1>

    <hr>

    <h2 class="text-success">1. Introduction to Background Image</h2>

    <p>
        A background image is an image that appears behind
        the content of a web page. It makes a website
        beautiful and attractive. Background images are
        commonly used in websites, home pages and banners.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-danger">2. Background Image Properties</h2>

    <p>
        CSS provides different properties to control
        background images. We can set the image size,
        position, repeat and attachment according to
        our website design.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-success">3. Background Image Repeat</h2>

    <p>
        The background-repeat property controls whether
        an image repeats horizontally or vertically.
        We can also stop the image from repeating.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-primary">4. Background Image Size</h2>

    <p>
        The background-size property controls the size
        of the background image. The cover value makes
        the image cover the entire background area.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-danger">5. Background Image Position</h2>

    <p>
        The background-position property controls
        where the background image appears.
        It can be placed at the top, bottom,
        center, left or right.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-success">6. Advantages of Background Image</h2>

    <ul>
        <li>Makes websites attractive.</li>
        <li>Improves website appearance.</li>
        <li>Creates beautiful web page designs.</li>
        <li>Useful for banners and home pages.</li>
        <li>Provides a professional look.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="text-primary">7. Conclusion</h2>

    <p>
        Background images are an important part of
        web designing. HTML, CSS and Bootstrap help
        us create beautiful and responsive websites.
        We can easily control background images
        using CSS properties.
    </p>

    <hr>

    <h3 class="text-center text-success">
        Thank You For Visiting!
    </h3>

</div>

